# HAProxy GeoIP country gating (example only - adapt and include
# from haproxy.cfg; nothing here loads automatically).
#
# 1. Fetch the database at runtime (license-keyed, weekly - never
#    vendored) and build the maps with the packaged tools:
#
#    geoipupdate -d /var/lib/geoip
#    haproxy-geoip-build-maps /var/lib/geoip/csv /etc/haproxy/geo
#
# 2. Frontend rules (map_ip returns UNKNOWN for unmapped ranges):
#
#    http-request set-var(txn.cc) src,map_ip(/etc/haproxy/geo/country-v4.map)
#    http-request set-var(txn.cc) src,map_ip(/etc/haproxy/geo/country-v6.map) if { var(txn.cc) -m str UNKNOWN }
#    http-request deny deny_status 403 if { var(txn.cc) -m str -f /etc/haproxy/geo/blocked-countries.lst }
#
# 3. Rebuild maps on the geoipupdate cadence (weekly cron) and
#    reload haproxy; map files are read at reload.
